    <dashboard name='IPF/PF Trial Stories' type='storyboard'>
      <layout-options>
        <title>
          <formatted-text>
            <run>fdfd</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </title>
      </layout-options>
      <style>
        <style-rule element='story-description'>
          <format attr='background-color' id='story-description_12' value='#00000000' />
          <format attr='border-width' id='story-description_12' value='0' />
          <format attr='border-style' id='story-description_12' value='none' />
          <format attr='background-color' id='story-description_11' value='#dfedeb6f' />
          <format attr='wrap' id='story-description_11' value='auto' />
          <format attr='text-align' id='story-description_11' value='auto' />
          <format attr='vertical-align' id='story-description_11' value='center' />
          <format attr='background-color' id='story-description_13' value='#f9e9e072' />
          <format attr='background-color' id='story-description_14' value='#00000000' />
          <format attr='border-width' id='story-description_14' value='0' />
          <format attr='border-style' id='story-description_14' value='none' />
          <format attr='background-color' id='story-description_15' value='#00000000' />
          <format attr='border-width' id='story-description_15' value='0' />
          <format attr='border-style' id='story-description_15' value='none' />
          <format attr='background-color' id='story-description_16' value='#dfedeb7e' />
          <format attr='border-width' id='story-description_16' value='1' />
          <format attr='border-style' id='story-description_16' value='solid' />
          <format attr='background-color' id='story-description_17' value='#00000000' />
          <format attr='border-width' id='story-description_17' value='0' />
          <format attr='border-style' id='story-description_17' value='none' />
          <format attr='background-color' id='story-description_18' value='#f5eddc6a' />
        </style-rule>
        <style-rule element='story-point-caption'>
          <format attr='width' value='959' />
        </style-rule>
      </style>
      <size maxheight='820' maxwidth='1216' minheight='820' minwidth='1216' preset-index='9' sizing-mode='fixed' />
      <zones>
        <zone h='100000' id='2' type-v2='layout-basic' w='100000' x='0' y='0'>
          <zone h='98048' id='9' param='vert' removable='false' type-v2='layout-flow' w='98684' x='658' y='976'>
            <zone h='98048' id='7' param='vert' removable='false' type-v2='layout-flow' w='98684' x='658' y='976'>
              <zone h='98048' id='1' param='vert' removable='false' type-v2='layout-flow' w='98684' x='658' y='976'>
                <zone fixed-size='107' h='9634' id='4' paired-zone-id='5' removable='false' type-v2='flipboard-nav' w='98684' x='658' y='976' />
                <zone h='88414' id='5' paired-zone-id='4' removable='false' type-v2='flipboard' w='98684' x='658' y='10610'>
                  <flipboard active-id='3' nav-type='number' show-nav-arrows='true'>
                    <story-points>
                      <story-point caption='Boehringer Ingelheim leads IPF/PF trial activity by a wide margin (45 trials, phase-weighted score of 86), reflecting its ownership of nintedanib. Notably, several of the most active sponsors — including Boehringer Ingelheim itself — are privately or family-owned, not publicly traded, which is factored into the color coding above and directly informs which sponsors will be trackable in the companion Earnings Surprise Tracker project.' captured-sheet='Sponsor Ranking' id='3' />
                      <story-point captured-sheet='Mechanism Performance' id='5' />
                      <story-point captured-sheet='Phase Funnel' id='6' />
                      <story-point captured-sheet='Risk Scores' id='7' />
                    </story-points>
                  </flipboard>
                </zone>
              </zone>
            </zone>
          </zone>
          <zone-style>
            <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
            <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
            <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
            <format attr='margin' value='8' />
          </zone-style>
        </zone>
        <zone flipboard-zone-id='5' forceUpdate='true' h='15244' id='11' story-point-id='3' type-v2='text' w='93997' x='2549' y='58049'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>Boehringer Ingelheim leads IPF/PF trial activity by a wide margin (45 trials, phase-weighted score of 86), reflecting its ownership of nintedanib. Notably, several of the most active sponsors — including Boehringer Ingelheim itself — are privately or family-owned, not publicly traded, which is factored into the color coding above and directly informs which sponsors will be trackable in the companion Earnings Surprise Tracker project.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone flipboard-zone-id='5' forceUpdate='true' h='3171' id='12' story-point-id='3' type-v2='text' w='23684' x='2303' y='1585'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true' fontsize='18'>1. Sponsor Ranking</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone flipboard-zone-id='5' h='17561' hidden='true' id='13' story-point-id='5' type-v2='text' w='94079' x='2796' y='42317'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='15'>Antifibrotic-mechanism trials combine strong performance (35.3% reach Phase 3+, 86.4% complete rather than terminate) with the largest reliable sample size (n=85) among established mechanism classes — consistent with antifibrotics being the only mechanism validated by FDA-approved IPF drugs. Categories like Endothelin Receptor Antagonist show higher raw percentages but on samples too small (n=7) to be statistically reliable.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone flipboard-zone-id='5' h='3415' hidden='true' id='14' story-point-id='5' type-v2='text' w='30757' x='2961' y='2439'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true' fontsize='18'>2. Mechanism Performance</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone flipboard-zone-id='5' forceUpdate='true' h='3415' hidden='true' id='15' story-point-id='6' type-v2='text' w='22286' x='63734' y='35000'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true' fontsize='18'>3. Phase Funnel</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone flipboard-zone-id='5' forceUpdate='true' h='38659' hidden='true' id='16' story-point-id='6' type-v2='text' w='40296' x='54934' y='46829'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='15'>IPF/PF trial volume peaks at Phase 2 (146 trials) and drops sharply at Phase 3 (62 trials, only 42.5% retained), reflecting how few candidates show strong enough Phase 2 efficacy signal to justify Phase 3&apos;s cost — a pattern consistent with IPF&apos;s historical difficulty to treat. Note: Early Phase 1 is a rarely-used exploratory step most programs skip, so the jump to Phase 1 reflects standard trial volume, not attrition.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone flipboard-zone-id='5' h='4024' hidden='true' id='17' story-point-id='7' type-v2='text' w='13240' x='3454' y='3171'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true' fontsize='18'>4. Risk Scores</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone flipboard-zone-id='5' h='23171' hidden='true' id='18' story-point-id='7' type-v2='text' w='93092' x='3207' y='60488'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='15'>A logistic regression model (ROC AUC 0.63, trained on 229 resolved trials) scored all 100 currently-active IPF/PF trials for termination risk. The highest-risk trials skew toward later phases (Phase 2/3), where efficacy is actually tested at scale — consistent with the Phase 3 attrition seen in the funnel view. Model performance is modest given the limited size of the training set (50 terminated trials), an honest constraint of small clinical trial datasets.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
      </zones>
      <simple-id uuid='{2622B111-2EB8-491B-B53A-CD0FA51B9D49}' />
    </dashboard>
  </dashboards>
